{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Source-of-truth square pool for Bingo Mode Phase 1. Move to SteamScraper/bingo_proto/phase1/squares.json at Stage 1 start.",
    "schema": {
      "name": "Square text shown on the tile",
      "mods_required": "Array of mod names. Empty = vanilla. Modded squares are excluded unless lobby toggles 'allow_modded'.",
      "verification": "'honor' | 'duel' | 'dice'. v1 includes honor and dice in the sampling pool; duel is parked for Phase 2.",
      "chapter": "Only on level_completion entries — display label from CHAPTERS in rush_data.py.",
      "stat_code": "Only on level_completion entries — Steam leaderboard stat code from rush_data.LEVELS."
    },
    "sections": ["standard", "level_completion", "modded"],
    "lobby_filtering": "Lobby settings pick which sections to draw from. Board = uniform random sample from union, filtered by allow_modded and verification in ('honor', 'dice') for v1.",
    "mods_referenced": ["Reverse Mode", "BoofOfMemes", "Challenge Deck", "NeonLite", "SecretShop", "NeonNetwork", "ChapterRush", "EventTracker"],
    "review_needed": [
      "mods_required tags in the modded section are best-effort. Worth a manual pass before Stage 1 — especially the EventTracker / NeonLite / SecretShop assignments which I inferred from square text rather than known mod docs.",
      "Square 'Kill any non-balloon demon without the use of a card during the level' — original list had no count. Left as worded; consider whether it should specify N levels.",
      "Square 'Complete any level with a comically small window size' — pure honor, no real verification path. Fine for v1, but worth flagging in the README so testers don't argue about what 'comically small' means.",
      "Squares 'Take a vacation to Idiot Island' and 'Let Red get away' — assumed honor. If they actually depend on a mod, retag.",
      "The Phase 1 chapter-without-discarding squares cover chapters 1,2,3,5,6,7,8,9. Chapters 4, 10, 11, 12 are intentionally absent in the user's list. Did not invent entries for them; can add later if desired."
    ]
  },

